WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:05.700
After season 7's staggering finale, viewers
were left with questions they never even anticipated.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:09.900
From ice dragons to Cleganebowl and the fate
of some of our favorite characters, here's

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:14.440
a spoiler filled look at all the questions
Game of Thrones needs to answer in its final

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:14.940
season.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:19.360
Ever since they first hatched, Daenerys' three
dragons have been an integral part of the

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:19.860
show.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:25.040
However, in Game of Thrones' most recent season,
one of Daenerys' dragons, Viserion, was felled

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.260
by the Night's King and fell under his thrall.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:31.120
So what does this undead dragon mean for Westeros
in the next season?

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:35.390
With so many theories floating around, it
can be hard to keep track, but fans can expect

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:37.100
a dragon showdown at the very least.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:42.660
Season 7's finale confirmed a long-held fan
theory that will seriously affect the final

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:47.780
season: Jon is not Ned Stark's bastard son,
but is instead a Targaryen, and the rightful

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:49.100
heir to the Iron Throne.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:53.680
That revelation means that Jon and Daenerys
are in for a nasty surprise, since they spent

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.440
the season 7 finale becoming very intimate.

00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:00.460
Considering that Jon has promised to help
Daenerys secure the Throne for herself, things

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:05.399
may get even more awkward when she realizes
her new lover isn't just her biggest rival...

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:06.540
he's also her nephew.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:11.811
So far, several names on Arya's infamous revenge
list have been killed by other people, and

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:13.810
she's personally taken down a few herself.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:15.440
"I want you to know that.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:21.479
The last thing you're ever going to see is
a Stark smiling down at you as you die."

00:01:21.479 --> 00:01:25.530
However, there are still several huge names
on her list that haven't yet been taken down.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:28.560
Though she thinks the Hound is dead, he's
actually still alive.

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:33.340
Likewise, the executioner who killed her father,
as well as big bads like The Mountain, Melisandre,

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:37.720
and Cersei Lannister are still on the loose
for Arya to hunt down.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:39.620
But will she be the one to end their lives?

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:44.860
Cersei Lannister has always been one of the
show's most despicable and complicated characters,

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:46.780
and currently, she holds the Iron Throne.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:50.540
In the last season, she dropped a big pregnancy-related
bombshell:

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:52.420
"We will defeat it.

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:57.480
For ourselves, for our house, for this."

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:03.900
As to the question of whether Cersei truly
is pregnant, Jeremy Podeswa, the director

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:08.020
of the season 7 finale, chimed in to say that
he believes that she wasn't lying.

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:13.250
But if she's telling the truth, it could hint
at her final fate, thanks to a handy prophecy.

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:15.660
"Will the king and I have children?"

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:18.430
"No, the king will have twenty children.

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:20.400
And you will have three."

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:23.000
Of course, Cersei already had three children.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:27.540
But in the books, this prophecy includes another
warning: that Cersei will be vanquished by

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:29.040
her valonqar, or little brother.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:33.480
Though Cersei has always assumed this means
Tyrion, Jaime is just a few minutes younger

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:34.260
than she is.

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:38.959
Many fans believe that if she really is pregnant
with his child, the pregnancy could cost Cersei

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:39.460
her life.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:44.740
Melisandre, the Red Woman, has been an increasingly
mysterious character on a show filled with

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:46.020
mysterious characters.

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:50.360
Even so, she's done her part when needed,
like when she raised Jon Snow from the dead

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:51.360
in season 6.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:55.980
In season 7, during a meeting with Varys,
the two agree that Melisandre should head

00:02:55.989 --> 00:02:56.989
to Volantis.

00:02:56.989 --> 00:02:58.840
"I will return, dear spider.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:00.900
One last time."

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:01.620
"M'lady…"

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:03.640
"I have to die in this strange country.

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:06.460
Just like you."

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:10.960
Although their conversation is riddled with
clues for superfans, it's hard to decipher

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:14.120
what role Melisandre will play in the show's
final season.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:18.620
Jaime Lannister might have become a fan favorite
over the course of the show's run, but he's

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:20.540
still a morally ambiguous character.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:24.760
However, through his journey with Brienne,
Jaime seems to have turned several corners.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:29.730
He even swore to fight against the White Walkers
rather than assist Cersei in her attempt to

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:30.730
shore power.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:34.800
Still, Jaime's always been loyal to his sister
when push comes to shove, so the question

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:38.239
remains: will he put aside petty squabbles
in the face of the White Walker invasion?

00:03:38.239 --> 00:03:40.650
Or will he stay a Lannister through and through?

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:42.540
Either way, he'll have a debt to pay.

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:50.140
"And of course, you have also heard the phrase,
'A Lannister always pays his debts.'"

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:55.560
One of the most anticipated showdowns in the
entirety of Game of Thrones is referred to

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:59.540
as Cleganebowl, which would see the Clegane
brothers pitted against each other.

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:03.560
The Mountain has become a brainless, mute
slave of Cersei, and the Hound has gone through

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:05.980
his own trials that's left him eager for revenge.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:09.859
Simply put, here's not much standing in the
way of these two fierce warriors duking it

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:10.360
out.

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:15.000
When the two reunited at the end of season
7, The Hound seemed to promise that Cleganebowl

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.260
was on the horizon.

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:17.460
"Doesn't matter.

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:20.740
That's not how it ends for you, brother.

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:23.000
You know who's coming for you.

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:25.660
You've always known."

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:31.280
It's still unclear what role Bran will play
in the final season, but naturally, fans have

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:32.300
plenty of ideas.

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:37.460
Fans have theorized that Bran exists in every
moment of time simultaneously or even that

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:41.380
Bran himself could actually be the mysterious
and powerful Night's King.

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:45.720
It's also possible that Bran was the catalyst
for the Mad King's descent into insanity.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:49.760
No matter what the answer is, it's clear that
Bran's role as the Three-Eyed Raven will have

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.720
a huge impact on final season.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:56.010
Some of the most meaningful moments on Game
of Thrones have come when beloved characters

00:04:56.010 --> 00:05:00.960
reunite after being separated for long periods,
and season seven looks to be full of these

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:01.460
moments.

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:06.220
One hotly awaited reunion is between Jon and
Arya Stark, two Starks who have always been

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:07.100
extremely close.

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:12.200
And fans are also curious to see if Arya and
the Hound reconnect after his supposed death.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:16.830
Likewise, who wouldn't want to see Sansa and
Tyrion reunite after their forced marriage

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:19.180
ended up with some unexpectedly sweet moments?

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:24.250
As the cast has dwindled, these long-awaited
reunions are sure to be some of the most emotional

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:25.700
moments in the series.

